    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Geospatial-Research-Lab-Assistant--Student-_R5073": {
      "title": "Geospatial Research Lab Assistant (Student)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWork Where You Learn: Build Experience, Grow Skills, and Contribute to Your University Community.   This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Most student positions at American University are eligible to use Federal Work Study (FWS) awards, with a few exceptions. FWS funds cannot be applied to janitorial, construction, partisan or sectarian positions. For information or questions regarding FWS funds, please contact American University's Office of Financial Aid.   Important guidance for current American University employees: American University current employees, including those employed in student positions, must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into your employee Workday account and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Applying outside of your employee Workday account may cause delays in a hire process. Department: Digital Research & Inquiry Lab Time Type: Part time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Job Description: Summary: The Student Geospatial Assistant will primarily be responsible for digitizing and georeferencing historical maps and data for use in academic research. Working with the Program Director for Geospatial Research Support in the University Library, the Student Geospatial Assistant will also help plan and run a creative mapping workshop and a community mapping event. No prior GIS experience is required; the Assistant will be trained in the core digitization skills the position uses and will gain hands-on experience with GIS software, data creation, metadata, and open-data publishing.   Essential Functions:  Georeferencing and digitizing historical maps. Extracting geographic features and building GIS data layers. Writing and publishing metadata. Assisting with the design and facilitation of a creative mapping workshop. Helping organize and run a Humanitarian OpenStreetMap (HOT) map-a-thon. Documenting digitization workflows for future use.   Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 10 hours per week. Salary Range: $18.40 per hour. Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or its equivalent. Must be a current AU Student.  Attention to detail and the ability to work independently once trained. An interest in maps, geography, history, data, or GIS.  Additional Eligibility Qualifications: Helpful but not required: familiarity with ArcGIS or QGIS, GitHub, coding, graphic design, or cartography. No prior GIS or mapping experience is required; training is provided. Approximately 10 hours per week, scheduled flexibly around the student's class schedule.   Other Details This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Visit https://www.american.edu/hr/ for additional information about American University employment and benefits.   Current American University Employees American University current employees (including those employed in student positions) must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings.   Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu .   American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/East-Campus-Washington-DC/Guest-Engagement-Coordinator_R5060-1": {
      "title": "Guest Engagement Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: Business Development Time Type: Full time Job Type: Regular FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Work Modality: Hybrid 01 (On Campus 3-4 Days/Week) Union: Excluded Job Description: Summary: Th Guest Engagement Coordinator is a member of the University Conference & Guest Services (UCGS) team within the division of Auxiliary Services and Finance. The Guest Engagement Coordinator will be the first point of contact for internal and external conference clients and guests and will manage UCGS communications as the initial point of contact. This person will be responsible for maintaining the UCGS website as well as data input within for the Intern Portal within Star Rez and Event Guru. This person will oversee all Intern housing components as well as other individual paying clients during the summer and will oversee year-round housing for Interns in Clark Hall. This position is also the sub-scheduler in EMS for the UCGS event spaces and will handle systems administration for Event Guru and Star Rez for Intern business.   Essential Functions: 1.) Communication Respond to initial inquiries about university conference and events. Approve or decline space reservations of UCGS spaces in EMS for Internal clients. Work with Director and Associate Director in gathering initial marketing information to maintain UCGS internal website, Destination DC and Unique Venues websites as well as other forms of Social Media. Produce informative weekly newsletter during summer months for Summer Student Staff. Assist Associate Director with the design and creation of UCGS marketing materials both on-line and hard copies. 2.) Guest Services Interpret client needs, anticipate potential problems, and determine the best solution for having a successful event. Keep detailed data in a customer relationship management system of all event planner information, as well as prospects gathered through various marketing strategies. Work with approximately 15 Intern and AU Internal Groups as well as 400 individual paying guests in the summer and 2-3 Intern Groups and 30 individual paying guest during the academic year by taking reservations, preparing contract information, working with the finance team with on-line payment and answering questions of each client. Serves as point person for UCGS and mail services to ensure data is prepared and disseminated so that clients may receive mail services  year-round. Provide visible, on-site coverage for clients as needed. 3.) Staff Recruitment, Selection, and Training and Supervision Support the University Conference & Guest Services team with summer student staff selection processes and training programs. Supervise (12-15) student staff  year-round. Supervise (1) Summer Leadership Student from January to August. 4.) Systems Administration Primary point of contact for administration of UCGS software solutions with Event Guru and Star Rez which are used in planning and preparing for Intern reservations, payment access as well as other services that include electronic access, security, and card production systems. Oversee the training and effective utilization of relevant UCGS software systems to ensure information in all systems is accurate, up-to-date, and audit compliant. Facilitate account access, training and troubleshooting support for all UCGS users when using Event Guru and Star Rez for Intern housing.   5.) Other Duties as Assigned   Supervisory Responsibility: Supervises 12-15 students year-round. Competencies: Displaying Creativity.   Prioritizing and Organizing. Serving Customers. Supporting Coworkers. Leading and Inspiring People. Making Accurate Judgments and Decisions. Building and Supporting Teams. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Full-time. 35 hours per week. Hours are 8am - 4pm or 9am - 5pm. Hybrid work modality (on campus 3 - 4 days per week). Requires some non-traditional hours during peak operational periods. Salary Range: $27.50 - $29.50 per hour. Required Education and Experience: Bachelor’s Degree. 1 - 3 years of relevant experience. At least one year of experience in event planning, university housing and/or summer conferences required. Computer experience, particularly in database and spreadsheet applications, required.  Must be able to prioritize, balance, and complete multiple tasks with direct but minimal supervision.  Excellent customer service skills required. Requires non-traditional hours during peak operational periods.   Preferred Education and Experience: Master's degree. Knowledge and experience with the following software programs: email, word processing, spreadsheet/data analysis and presentation development software applications such as Microsoft Outlook, Word, Excel, EMS, STAR REZ and Event Guru. Supervision of paraprofessional staff. Other Duties: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Benefits AU offers a competitive benefits package.  Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/4401-Connecticut-Campus-Washington-DC/Writer-Editor_R5056": {
      "title": "Writer/Editor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: Community Communications Time Type: Full time Job Type: Regular FLSA Status: Exempt Work Modality: Hybrid 01 (On Campus 3-4 Days/Week) Union: SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division This position is part of a collective bargaining unit represented by SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division. That means the terms and conditions of your employment are governed by university policy (including the Staff Personnel Policies Manual) and any collective bargaining agreement entered into between American University and SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division. Job Description: Summary: The Writer/Editor identifies, pitches, and crafts compelling, high-impact stories across American University’s flagship enterprise channels. Working closely with the editor and a dynamic creative team of designers, videographers, and photographers, this role drives community-centered storytelling, transforming institutional milestones, research breakthroughs, and individual voices into vibrant narratives for diverse audiences—including prospective and current students, alumni, faculty, staff, donors, and more. In this role, the Writer/Editor researches, reports, and writes engaging content for American magazine, the weekly AU Now newsletter, university web pages, marketing campaigns, and multimedia scripts. The position executes an array of storytelling formats—including in-depth narrative features, profiles, research stories, institutional news, trend pieces, and event coverage (including occasional evenings and weekends). The Writer/Editor experiments with fresh narrative formats, distinct angles, and creative storytelling techniques tailored to shifting audience interests and digital reading habits. Additionally, they deliver polished, accurate, and fact-checked copy on deadline, maintain a consistent brand voice across all media, and actively contribute to pitch meetings, long-term editorial planning, and cross-functional creative strategy to bring the AU story to life. The ideal candidate brings a demonstrated track record of reporting and writing versatile, engaging stories across print and digital platforms, supported by exceptional interviewing, research, and narrative development skills. They think boldly, embrace creative risk-taking, and pivot seamlessly between fast-turnaround assignments and long-form features. Strong project management skills, meticulous attention to nuance, and a commitment to producing clean copy under tight deadlines are essential, as is a collaborative mindset honed by partnering with visual creatives such as designers, photographers, and videographers. A background in copyediting and proofreading (The Chicago Manual of Style) or multimedia production (scriptwriting, video, or social) is a strong plus. Essential Functions: 1.) Content Reporting and Development Identify, report, and write a wide range of print and multimedia content for American University’s flagship enterprise channels, including American magazine, AU Now, university web pages, marketing campaigns, and multimedia scripts. Research story ideas, develop interview questions, cultivate on- and off-the-record sources, and produce clear, concise, and colorful copy for assignments ranging from 200-word department pieces to 3,000-word features to a holiday video script. Copyedit and proofread content as needed. 2.) Editorial Planning and Source Cultivation Collaborate closely with the editor to brainstorm story concepts, plan dynamic editorial calendars, and develop enterprise packages for the university. Identify students, faculty, staff, alumni, and community members with compelling narratives; cultivate a robust network of sources across campus and beyond; conduct background research; and track emerging trends in higher education, alumni communications, and digital media. 3.) Digital Production and CMS Support Build and publish stories within the content management system (CMS), assisting with the ongoing maintenance and digital presentation of the university’s news and magazine sites. 4.) Other Duties as Assigned Support broader university communications initiatives and perform other related editorial or creative duties as needed. Competencies: Displaying Creativity. Prioritizing and Organizing. Making Accurate Judgments and Decisions. Evaluating and Implementing Ideas. Developing Plans. Thinking Broadly. Supporting Coworkers. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Full-time. 35 hours per week. Hybrid work modality (three days in the office). Salary Range: $70,000.00 - $75,000.00 annually. Required Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree or equivalent. 5 - 8 years of relevant experience. At least five years of professional writing experience—preferably with a news outlet or higher education institution. Preferred Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree. 8 - 10 years of relevant experience. Additional Eligibility Qualifications: Strong writing, copyediting, and proofreading skills, along with familiarity with videography, social media, and digital publishing. Self-starter with an entrepreneurial approach to their work, capable of juggling competing priorities and deadlines while thriving under pressure. Confident interviewer and savvy researcher. Excellent news judgment, strong diplomacy skills, and ease in both academic and non-academic settings. Proven ability to write compelling, accurate content in a variety of styles for diverse audiences. Collegial and flexible team player who brings empathy, a collaborative spirit, and a good sense of humor. Ability to seamlessly transition from interviewing the university president for a magazine feature to shooting tiny-mic videos with students on the quad. Other Duties: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Benefits AU offers a competitive benefits package.  Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/4401-Connecticut-Campus-Washington-DC/XMLNAME-1A-Plus-Podcast-Producer--Producer-I-_R4939": {
      "title": "1A Plus Podcast Producer (Producer I)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: Production Time Type: Full time Job Type: Regular FLSA Status: Exempt Work Modality: Hybrid 01 (On Campus 3-4 Days/Week) Union: Screen Actors Guild - American Federation of Television and Radio Artists (SAG-AFTRA) This position is part of a collective bargaining unit represented by the Screen Actors Guild - American Federation of Television and Radio Artists (SAG-AFTRA).This position is part of a collective bargaining unit represented by the Screen Actors Guild - American Federation of Television and Radio Artists (SAG-AFTRA). Job Description: Summary: WAMU 88.5 is a public media station owned and operated by American University. WAMU is the source for local, regional and NPR news and original programs in Washington DC. Since 1961, WAMU has been amplifying voices and sharing stories from the many neighborhoods and communities in the District of Columbia, Maryland and Virginia. The 1A Podcast/ Plus Producer is responsible for the integrated daily production and distribution of both the 1A podcast and 1A Plus products (versions of the daily program created for member stations that don’t air 1A live), ensuring timely and uninterrupted delivery to both broadcast and digital audiences. Working under the direction of the Senior Supervising Producer, this individual serves as the primary producer responsible for the daily preparation, editing and distribution of these products This includes re-packaging and re-editing content from the live version of 1A that airs each morning to ensure it a) meets the needs of the dozens of broadcast stations that air 1A Plus across multiple time zones and b) that the broadcast program is appropriately edited to meet the differing expectations of the on-demand podcast audience. The producer edits content as needed, coordinates host retracks, ensures the various products meet all timing requirements, and incorporates sponsorship messages, funding credits, and other required program elements. In addition, the Podcast/Plus producer uploads and distributes both podcast and Plus versions, ensuring all deadlines are met.    This position reports to the Senior Supervising Producer, 1A.     Essential Functions : 1.) Produces and Edits the Daily 1A Plus and 1A Podcast Products Repackages and re-edits the live 1A broadcast into products tailored for both member station and on-demand podcast audiences. Edits and assembles program content, including pacing, timing, and flow while preserving the editorial integrity of the original program. Supervises host retracks and incorporates sponsorship messages, funding credits, and other required program elements. Ensures all products meet editorial, broadcast, and technical quality standards. 2.) Performs the Technical Production, Quality Control, and Distribution of the Daily 1A Plus and Podcast Products Oversee final production workflows to ensure timely and uninterrupted delivery across broadcast and digital platforms. Performs final quality assurance and verifies all timing and formatting requirements are met. Uploads, publishes, and distributes podcast and 1A Plus products according to established production schedules and deadlines. Troubleshoots production and distribution issues to ensure reliable daily delivery. 3.) Supports the overall production of other 1A programming, with specific responsibilities for producing Rebroadcasts (shows re-aired on holidays etc.) and Evergreen Editions (the regularly updated emergency programs provided to stations in case of significant technical difficulties). 4.) Provides guidance and technical assistance to 1A staff and collaborators regarding podcast and 1A Plus production workflows and serves as a resource to support operational continuity. Competencies: Serving Customers. Displaying Creativity. Prioritizing and Organizing. Acquiring and Analyzing Information. Supporting Coworkers. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Full-time. 35 hours per week. Hybrid work modality (3 - 4 days per week in office). Salary Range: $68,656.00 annually. Required Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree or equivalent. 1 - 3 years of relevant experience. Experience in audio production, journalism, broadcast production, or a related field. High level of aptitude with audio editing and sound design, with a firm grasp of one or more editing platforms. Experience of and aptitude for working on tight daily deadlines. Strong communication skills, with the ability to offer and accept constructive feedback. Highly organized, experience setting up audio file inventories and tracking tape assets. Demonstrates an interest in mentoring other teammates, including freelancers and interns. Strong writing skills and editorial judgment. Experience using multimedia content production and other online tools to edit photos, audio, and video, (WordPress, Adobe, Final Cut Pro). Experience working with content management systems (CMS). Proven ability to work collaboratively as part of a team. Driven and determined, demonstrated creative problem-solving skills. Keen understanding of national and international current events, and excellent news and narrative judgment. Time management skills, flexibility, and ability to work effectively in a dynamic, unpredictable news environment. Committed to creating an inclusive and respectful workplace and team environment. Preferred Education and Experience: 3 - 5 years of relevant experience. Other Duties: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Benefits AU offers a competitive benefits package.  Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Tenley-Campus-Washington-DC/Part-Time-Career-Counselor_R4881": {
      "title": "Part-Time Career Counselor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: Washington College of Law Time Type: Part time Job Type: Regular FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Work Modality: Union: SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division This position is part of a collective bargaining unit represented by SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division. That means the terms and conditions of your employment are governed by university policy (including the Staff Personnel Policies Manual) and any collective bargaining agreement entered into between American University and SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division. Job Description: Summary:   The Part-Time Career Counselor provides individualized and group law student advising, identifies and develops resources for students and alumni, and designs and presents educational programs and events. Each Career Counselor also assists with other counseling and programming initiatives of the Washington College of Law (WCL) Office of Career & Professional Development (OCPD), including serving as the liaison between the office and assigned WCL programs, institutes, student groups, and other internal and external organizations and associations.  The Career Counselor may also develop additional specialties as needed, such as sector- or practice area-specific expertise. The Career Counselor will work closely with a team that includes counselors, recruiting professionals, and administrative employees.       Essential Functions:   1.) Career Advising Advise law students on all aspects of career planning and job search methods, including self-assessment, resumes, cover letters, interviewing and networking to aid students in their job searches and career development.   2.) Programming Develop and facilitate job search skill development workshops and other educational programs and initiatives. Identify content areas and coordinate seminars, panel discussions, and other resources that meet the needs of students interested in a broad range of employment sectors and practice areas.      3.) Industry Analysis and Engagement Analyze legal trends and develop employer networks based on student and office needs. Use employer contacts to gather information about job and hiring trends and inquire about internships and employment possibilities. Use knowledge gained to educate other members of the OCPD staff and incorporate knowledge during individual counseling sessions with students. Work with OCPD’s recruiting team members to conduct outreach and create interactive opportunities between OCPD and employers.      4.) Professional Development Participate in professional organizations related to career counseling and legal employment. Review publications to keep abreast of job market trends including the National Law Journal/Legal Times and in-house counsel publications.    5.) Other Tasks Assist the Senior Director and other team members with counseling, programming, outreach, and engagement as directed. Work closely with fellow counselors to ensure consistent messaging under the guidance of the Senior Director. Complete projects as tasked to assist with the overall goals of the office.     Supervisory Responsibility: May supervise student and/or administrative staff.   Competencies: Championing Customer Needs.  Developing Plans. Making Accurate Judgments and Decisions.    Evaluating and Implementing Ideas.  Building and Supporting Teams.    Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 27 hours per week. Some evening and weekend hours are required.   Salary Range: $35.00 - $40.00 per hour. Required Education and Experience: Juris Doctor or equivalent. 2 - 4 years of relevant experience, w hich may include legal experience, recruiting experience and/or counseling experience.   Preferred Education and Experience:  Juris Doctor.    3 - 5 years of relevant experience.     Travel Required: Periodic travel for professional conferences is required.    Additional Eligibility Qualifications: We strongly encourage applicants to submit a resume and cover letter describing their interest in and qualifications for the position. Must possess excellent interpersonal, organizational and oral, and written communication skills. Knowledge of job search, career/ employment services, recruiting, interviewing and staffing principles and practices.  Must have a broad understanding of career counseling techniques with specific knowledge of legal market trends and job search strategies.  Ability to assess individual needs, motivators and differences in abilities and career interests, including those in the public and private sectors. Must be comfortable working in a fast-paced environment and marketing the Washington College of Law to employers. Other Duties:   Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time, with or without notice. Benefits Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Part-Time-Hourly-Fitness-Instructor_R5048": {
      "title": "Part-Time Hourly Fitness Instructor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: Group Exercise Time Type: Part time Job Type: Casual FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Work Modality: Union: Excluded Job Description: Summary: Group fitness instructors will lead members, in a group environment, through safe and effective fitness classes for Campus Recreational Services. This position is responsible for providing group exercise fitness instruction and supervision in variety of formats. Candidates must be able to instruct multiple fitness levels and ensure the safety of all patrons in the class. We are currently looking for a Pilates Instructor. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 3 hours per week. Salary Range: $24.00 - $44.00 per hour. Required Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree or equivalent. 1 - 3 years of relevant experience. Current CPR/AED certified. At least one nationally recognized and accredited group exercise certification. Preferred Education and Experience: 2 - 4 years of relevant experience. Experience in group exercise instruction and/or administration. Benefits Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
