    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/PASS-Program-Tutor--Student-_R5010": {
      "title": "PASS Program Tutor (Student)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-22\nPosted: Posted 20 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWork Where You Learn: Build Experience, Grow Skills, and Contribute to Your University Community.   This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Most student positions at American University are eligible to use Federal Work Study (FWS) awards, with a few exceptions. FWS funds cannot be applied to janitorial, construction, partisan or sectarian positions. For information or questions regarding FWS funds, please contact American University's Office of Financial Aid.   Important guidance for current American University employees: American University current employees, including those employed in student positions, must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into your employee Workday account and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Applying outside of your employee Workday account may cause delays in a hire process. Department: Student Academic Services Time Type: Part time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Job Description: Summary: PASS Tutors offer one-on-one tutoring support to students through AU’s Peer Assisted Student Support (PASS) Program. The PASS Program is free to all AU students, and paid peer tutors are also AU students! Essential Functions:   Provide one-on-one tutoring in their supported courses.  Adequately prepare for tutoring sessions by reviewing WCOnline appointment forms, and reviewing past concepts during shifts. Use empty sessions to complete other role-related tasks and activities. Distribute Post-Tutoring Survey to their attendees at the end of each session.  Complete Post-Appointment Client Report Forms after tutoring sessions.  Attend and fully participate in semester trainings.  Conduct peer observations of fellow PASS Program Tutors.  Meet with Tutoring staff at least twice per semester.  Accurately complete time sheets and surveys in a timely manner.   Conduct class visits to advertise the PASS Program to students across campus. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 2 - 6 hours per week. Salary Range: $18.40 - $20.00 per hour. Additional Eligibility Qualifications:   Work up to 6 hours per week (unless otherwise approved by Tutoring staff). Tutors will likely be scheduled between 2 - 4 hours per week to start the semester.  Positions renew each semester based upon Tutor feedback, student feedback, course offerings, and American University enrollment status.  PASS Program Tutors must retain a cumulative GPA at or above 3.0, from the start of employment until date of separation. Failure to do so can result in suspension or termination from the role. In addition to pay, PASS Program Tutors will have opportunities for professional development and skills development throughout the semester as Peer Tutors.  PASS tutors are part of a community of fellow tutors on campus who have various backgrounds of study.  Before applying on Workday, please see our website for the full application process. Other Details This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Visit https://www.american.edu/hr/ for additional information about American University employment and benefits.   Current American University Employees American University current employees (including those employed in student positions) must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings.   Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu .   American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Student-Athlete-Support-Program--SASP-Tutor--Student-_R5008": {
      "title": "Student-Athlete Support Program, SASP Tutor (Student)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-22\nPosted: Posted 20 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWork Where You Learn: Build Experience, Grow Skills, and Contribute to Your University Community.   This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Most student positions at American University are eligible to use Federal Work Study (FWS) awards, with a few exceptions. FWS funds cannot be applied to janitorial, construction, partisan or sectarian positions. For information or questions regarding FWS funds, please contact American University's Office of Financial Aid.   Important guidance for current American University employees: American University current employees, including those employed in student positions, must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into your employee Workday account and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Applying outside of your employee Workday account may cause delays in a hire process. Department: SASP Support Time Type: Part time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Job Description: Summary: The Student-Athlete Support Program (SASP) provides free, virtual peer tutoring services in a one-on-one format to all student-athletes in historically challenging courses defined by student needs and tutoring requests. SASP tutors build and reinforce academic skills and knowledge needed for most core programs at AU. Tutors model effective study habits and learning strategies, equipping student athletes with the skills and knowledge to work and succeed independent of the tutor. Essential Functions: Provide virtual and/or in-person one-on-one tutoring, determined by course and student needs. Adequately prepare for tutoring sessions by completing the SASP Canvas tutorial course. Complete the post-session notes outlining content and concepts covered, progress made, and/or challenges encountered in tutoring sessions. Accurately complete time sheets in a timely manner. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 8 hours per week. Salary Range: $18.40 - $20.00 per hour. Required Education and Experience: Enrollment in a degree program at American University. Maintenance of a cumulative 3.0 GPA. Demonstrate course mastery by receiving an A or A- in their supported course. Willingness to work with diverse populations of faculty, staff, and students. Demonstrate excellent written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to work collaboratively in professional team environments. Possess strong organizational skills and experience in basic office management. Ability to work independently and take initiative. Ability to maintain an appropriate degree of confidentiality. Possess intermediate computer skills in Microsoft Office Suite. Additional Eligibility Qualifications: This position renews on a semester basis based upon student need, enrollment data, and course requests. Benefits: professional development opportunities, peer Leader experience. Other Details This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Visit https://www.american.edu/hr/ for additional information about American University employment and benefits.   Current American University Employees American University current employees (including those employed in student positions) must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings.   Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu .   American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Equity---Title-IX-Investigator_R4968": {
      "title": "Equity & Title IX Investigator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-22\nPosted: Posted 20 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: Equity & Title IX Operations Time Type: Full time Job Type: Regular FLSA Status: Exempt Work Modality: Hybrid 01 (On Campus 3-4 Days/Week) Union: Excluded Job Description: Summary:   The Investigator is responsible for managing the day-to-day responsibilities associated with the University’s Equity and Title IX Office. Working under the overall supervision of the Assistant Vice President for Equity and Title IX Coordinator and directly for the Director for Equity and Deputy Title IX Coordinator, the Investigator will have primary responsibility for investigating and producing comprehensive reports regarding complaints of discrimination, harassment, sexual misconduct and retaliation by students, faculty or staff. This includes interviewing parties and witnesses, collecting evidence, and drafting high-quality investigation reports and documents within established timelines, and making finding of facts to resolve complaints, in accordance with the University’s discrimination policies. The Equity and Title IX Investigator will also participate in assessing incoming reports and complaints, making recommendations regarding supportive measures, and assist in implementing training and education focused on Title VII, Title VI, Title IX, Section 504, and other federal and/or local civil rights laws. Essential Functions: 1.) Assessment and Investigation Initial assessment includes collaborating in reviewing reports and complaints in a timely manner to ensure a prompt response and evaluating the need for supportive measures, assistance and resources for individuals engaged in the process. Conduct prompt and thorough investigations, including development of an investigation plan, drafting notice of investigations and other essential correspondence, identifying and interviewing witnesses, gathering information and data, keeping accurate and thorough records and notes of the investigation process, applying the policy, and preparing a detailed report with an analysis,  and a finding based on a preponderance of the evidence, where the policy calls for the investigator to make a finding. Responsible for managing all communications with parties, advisors and witnesses. Assures compliance with timelines, acts as an impartial party, maintains a high level of confidentiality and discretion, and ensures a prompt, fair and neutral process for all parties. As the assigned investigator in cases of complaints alleging all forms of discrimination as defined by federal and local law, and all forms of sexual misconduct, including sexual harassment, sexual violence and dating and domestic violence, the incumbent completes complex investigations with a great deal of independence with respect to the day-to-day tasks that must be completed. 2.) Training, Outreach and Education Assist in the development and implementation of educational materials and training for faculty, staff and students regarding compliance with Title VII, Title VI, Title IX, VAWA, the ADA and other federal and local laws and regulations, and assist in outreach activities designed to communicate the responsibilities of the Equity and Title IX Office. Collaborate with the Office of Inclusive Excellence to ensure University training and engagement efforts are implemented. 3.) Monitor Legal Developments and Best Practices Stay abreast of developments in law, policy and best practices related to employment and education discrimination and harassment and investigation processes. Engage in required trainings to ensure skills and knowledge are current. Other duties as assigned. Competencies: Evaluating and Implementing Ideas. Making Accurate Judgments and Decisions. Building and Supporting Teams. Championing Customer Needs. Developing Plans. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Full-time. 35 hours per week. Hybrid work modality. Salary Range: $93,771.00 - $100,000.00 annually. Required Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree. 5 or more years of related experience conducting prompt, thorough, and equitable investigations regarding allegations of harassment, discrimination, sexual misconduct, and sexual violence or the equivalent legal experience OR a Juris Doctor plus 2 or more years of related experience conducting prompt, thorough, and equitable investigations regarding allegations of harassment, discrimination, sexual misconduct, and sexual violence or the equivalent legal experience. Preferred Education and Experience: Juris Doctor. 8 - 10 years of relevant experience. Requisite knowledge, training and experience related to federal and local discrimination laws and related regulations, such as Title VII, Title VI, Title IX, ADA and the ADEA, as well as VAWA, strongly preferred. Experience working in higher education preferred. Travel Required: On campus or within the Washington, DC area. Additional Eligibility Qualifications: Experience handling confidential information with tact, discretion, and sensitivity. Demonstrated strong skill in writing concise, logical analytical reports to convey complex issues. Strong interpersonal and presentation skills. Strong organizational and analytical skills. Cross-cultural competency. Must be comfortable with technology, including maintaining content on websites and identifying and vetting online training programs. Excellent interpersonal and organizational skills. Other Duties: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Benefits AU offers a competitive benefits package.  Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Marketing-Assistant--Student-_R5003": {
      "title": "Marketing Assistant (Student)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWork Where You Learn: Build Experience, Grow Skills, and Contribute to Your University Community.   This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Most student positions at American University are eligible to use Federal Work Study (FWS) awards, with a few exceptions. FWS funds cannot be applied to janitorial, construction, partisan or sectarian positions. For information or questions regarding FWS funds, please contact American University's Office of Financial Aid.   Important guidance for current American University employees: American University current employees, including those employed in student positions, must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into your employee Workday account and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Applying outside of your employee Workday account may cause delays in a hire process. Department: College of Arts & Sciences Time Type: Part time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Job Description: Summary: Open exclusively to AU students, the Marketing and Publications Assistant works closely with the American University Museum’s Marketing and Publications Specialist to support social media, marketing, and communications for the museum’s seasonal exhibitions and programs. The primary focus of this position is social media marketing. The assistant will gather information and materials from artists, curators, and museum staff; identify the most compelling aspects of exhibitions and programs; and translate that information into engaging, accessible promotional content for museum audiences. Responsibilities include developing a strategic social media schedule, writing promotional copy, creating and sourcing visual content, photographing exhibitions and events, and scheduling posts in advance through Hootsuite. The position may also assist with email marketing and developing promotional content for email campaigns. This role is well suited to a creative, responsible, and self-directed student who can work effectively in an environment where priorities and assignments may evolve. The ideal candidate is comfortable taking initiative, making thoughtful decisions about content, and keeping the Marketing and Publications Specialist informed about the status of ongoing projects, questions, and deadlines. Essential Functions: Gather information and materials from artists, curators, and museum staff. Identify the most compelling aspects of exhibitions and programs and translate that information into engaging, accessible promotional content for museum audiences. Develop a strategic social media schedule. Write promotional copy. Create and source visual content. Photograph exhibitions and events. Schedule posts in advance through Hootsuite. Assist with email marketing and developing promotional content for email campaigns. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 10 - 15 hours per week. Salary Range: $18.40 - $23.50 per hour. Preferred Education and Experience: Marketing, public relations, communications, art, and art history students are especially encouraged to apply. Excellent writing skills, with an ability to identify the most important and compelling information in longer written materials and transform it into concise, engaging promotional copy. Knowledge of social media marketing and an understanding of how content and messaging can be adapted for different audiences. Strong visual judgment and a good design aesthetic; proficiency in Canva required. Experience with Adobe Creative Suite is desirable. Highly responsible, organized, and attentive to deadlines. Able to work independently and effectively in a flexible, sometimes unstructured environment. Strong communication skills, including a willingness to provide regular status updates, ask questions when needed, and flag potential problems before deadlines are affected. Comfortable communicating professionally with artists, curators, museum staff, and other collaborators. Photography and social media video experience is a plus. Additional Eligibility Qualifications: Hybrid position, approximately 15 hours per week, with a combination of on-site work at the museum and remote work. Occasional weekend hours may be requested to photograph, film, or attend museum events. Museum marketing is deadline-driven and often involves managing several projects at once. The successful candidate must be dependable, organized, and proactive about communicating progress, questions, potential problems, and anticipated delays. Other Details This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Visit https://www.american.edu/hr/ for additional information about American University employment and benefits.   Current American University Employees American University current employees (including those employed in student positions) must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings.   Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu .   American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/ATEC-Studio-Assistant--Student---FWS-_R4983": {
      "title": "ATEC Studio Assistant (Student) (FWS)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWork Where You Learn: Build Experience, Grow Skills, and Contribute to Your University Community.   This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Most student positions at American University are eligible to use Federal Work Study (FWS) awards, with a few exceptions. FWS funds cannot be applied to janitorial, construction, partisan or sectarian positions. For information or questions regarding FWS funds, please contact American University's Office of Financial Aid.   Important guidance for current American University employees: American University current employees, including those employed in student positions, must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into your employee Workday account and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Applying outside of your employee Workday account may cause delays in a hire process. Department: College of Arts & Sciences Time Type: Part time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Job Description: Summary: The Audio Technology Program seeks a part-time undergraduate work-study ATEC Studio Assistant to support day-to-day operations in the ATEC Recording Studio. The candidate must have completed or be currently enrolled in ATEC 415/615, Sound Studio Techniques. In addition, we seek an individual who demonstrates strong organizational skills, is punctual, detail oriented, and has the ability to manage multiple priorities in a dynamic and creative environment. Essential Functions: Support day-to-day operations in the ATEC Recording Studio. Other duties as assigned. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 6 hours per week. Salary Range: $18.40 per hour. Required Education and Experience: Current AU student with an active Federal Work Study (FWS) award. The candidate must have completed or be currently enrolled in ATEC 415/615, Sound Studio Techniques. Demonstrate strong organizational skills, is punctual, detail oriented, and has the ability to manage multiple priorities in a dynamic and creative environment. Other Details This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Visit https://www.american.edu/hr/ for additional information about American University employment and benefits.   Current American University Employees American University current employees (including those employed in student positions) must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings.   Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu .   American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
